# Server-side configuration for the two Vercel Functions in api/.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE AND IS COMMITTED. Never put real values in it.
# Real values go in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables), or in a local `.env` — which `.gitignore` already excludes via the
# `*.local` / dotfile rules. Check before you create one.
#
# ⚠ None of these are read by the browser. They are read only inside
# `api/subscribe.ts` and `api/contact.ts`, which run on Vercel's Node runtime.
# Astro's `PUBLIC_` prefix is deliberately NOT used anywhere here — a PUBLIC_
# variable is inlined into the client bundle and would publish the Mailchimp key.

# --- Newsletter → Mailchimp (api/subscribe.ts) -------------------------------
#
# ⚠ Until BOTH of these are set, /api/subscribe answers 503 and the newsletter
# reports a neutral failure. Set them BEFORE flipping NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT to
# '/api/subscribe' in src/content/site.ts, or the form ships broken to everyone.
#
# Mailchimp → Account & billing → Extras → API keys.
# The key ends in its datacenter, e.g. "…-us21".
MAILCHIMP_API_KEY=

# Mailchimp → Audience → Settings → "Audience name and defaults" → Audience ID.
# Ten-ish hex characters, e.g. "a1b2c3d4e5". NOT the audience name.
MAILCHIMP_AUDIENCE_ID=

# Optional. The datacenter is derived from the suffix of the API key, so leave
# this empty unless a key ever arrives without one.
MAILCHIMP_SERVER_PREFIX=

# --- Contact form → HubSpot (api/contact.ts) ---------------------------------
#
# Neither of these is secret — they appear in HubSpot's own public embed code —
# but they live here anyway so the vendor stays out of the page source and
# swapping CRM touches no client file.
#
# The number in any HubSpot app URL while logged in, e.g. app.hubspot.com/…/12345678/…
HUBSPOT_PORTAL_ID=

# HubSpot → Marketing → Forms → open the form → the GUID in the URL.
# ⚠ The HubSpot form's internal field names must match the `name` attributes in
# src/content/contact.ts FIELDS. HubSpot silently DROPS values whose property it
# does not recognise — a submission can succeed with fields missing and nothing
# reports it. Send one test submission and check every field arrived.
HUBSPOT_FORM_GUID=
